.TH WMNOTIFY 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmnotify \- freedesktop notification daemon that follows the Window Maker theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmnotify
.SH DESCRIPTION
Owns the D-Bus name org.freedesktop.Notifications on the session bus and shows each notification as a small pop-up
drawn like a Window Maker menu: the summary in a title bar (MenuTitleBack, MenuTitleColor, MenuTitleFont) over the
body (MenuTextBack, MenuTextColor, MenuTextFont). Gradients and Xft fonts are used as the theme gives them.
Critical notifications use the highlight colours and stay until clicked. The theme is re-read while pop-ups are
visible, so a theme change restyles them.
.PP
Supported: icons (the \fBimage-path\fR hint, the icon name, or the application's own icon), action buttons
(\fBActionInvoked\fR, \fBNotificationClosed\fR), \fBurgency\fR, \fBvalue\fR (progress bar), replacing by id, and the
markup tags <b>, <i>, <u> and <a> in the body (other tags are dropped). Hovering a pop-up pauses its timeout.
Clicking the body dismisses it, or invokes the "default" action if the sender offered one. At most eight are shown.
Only one notification daemon can run; a second instance exits with status 1.
.SH SETTINGS
Set with \fBwmsettings set\fR; they apply to the next notification.
.TP
.B notify_corner
top-right (default), top-left, bottom-right or bottom-left.
.TP
.B notify_timeout
Default timeout in milliseconds (default 5000).
.TP
.B notify_dnd
\fBon\fR hides everything except critical notifications (they are still recorded in the history).
.TP
.B notify_mute
Comma-separated application names that never pop up (case-insensitive).
.TP
.B notify_app_timeout
Comma-separated \fIapp\fR:\fIms\fR pairs: default timeout for applications that do not set one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/wm-desktop/notify-history
Every notification received, one tab-separated line each, trimmed at 256 KB. Overridden by $WMNOTIFY_HISTORY.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmnotify-send (1),
.BR wmnotifyctl (1),
.BR wmsettings (1),
.BR wm-autostart (1)
